IMPORT prelude

-- Census Act 1973 (Singapore) -- what a census asks of an occupier, an institution or an employer (ss 7(2), 8, 10, 11, 14), how long
-- an officer may come back to check (s 10(4)), what may be done with the answers (ss 13, 17, 18, 23), and the offences and penalties
-- (ss 18(4), 19, 20, 21, 22).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CA1973.txt. The deposit says it "incorporates all
-- amendments up to and including 1 December 2021" and came into operation on 31 December 2021; its Legislative History lists Act 15
-- of 2010 (Criminal Procedure Code 2010) as the last amending Act, followed by the 2013 Revised Edition. The SSO record retrieved on
-- 1 October 2026 calls it the current version. FOLLOWS THE BODY'S SECTION NUMBERS: the arrangement at the top of the deposit is one
-- out of step (it lists "Occupier to allow access" as s 9; the body has it as s 8).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0128 in ../../../requirements.jsonl: Tier 2 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by
-- everyday-life relevance. The requirement asks what the Act decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked
-- a sharper question yet. SCOPED to the duties a household, a hotel or institution, or an employer meets when a census is taken,
-- the confidentiality of what they give, and the offences. Not encoded: the power to direct a census (s 3), appointments (ss 4-6),
-- enumeration of the forces and of people not living in a house (s 12), the duty of Government employees to assist (s 15), the
-- internal flow of schedules (s 16), the Minister's duty about trade secrets (s 17(5)), rules (s 24), amendment of the Schedules
-- (s 25) and the transitional provision (s 26). No census notification or rules made under s 24 were retrieved, so "the time
-- mentioned" in a schedule and any "prescribed" longer checking period are inputs, not facts.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Census Act 1973 -- duties, confidentiality and offences`

GIVEN `the first` IS A NUMBER, `the second` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the larger of` MEANS
    IF `the first` GREATER THAN `the second` THEN `the first` ELSE `the second`

§§ `8 and 10 -- the occupier`

-- s 8: "Every person occupying any dwelling house or other premises must allow any census officer such access ... as may be
-- necessary for the purposes of a census", and must allow the officer to "paint, mark or affix" letters, marks or numbers.
-- s 2: a "dwelling house" is a building "wholly or partly used for the purpose of human habitation and includes any ship or vessel
-- in Singapore".
-- s 10(2): the occupier "must, within the time mentioned therein, fill in the schedule, or cause it to be filled in, in the manner
-- prescribed and must thereafter deliver the schedule" to an enumerator, a supervisor or whoever the Superintendent directs.
-- (3): an occupier "unable either to fill in the schedule or cause it to be filled in" must "preserve it in the condition he or she
-- received it" and deliver it; the officer then asks the questions (s 9) and fills it in.
GIVEN `filled in and delivered within the time` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `unable to fill it in` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `preserved it unfilled and delivered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier has complied with the schedule` IF
        `filled in and delivered within the time`
    OR  (`unable to fill it in` AND `preserved it unfilled and delivered it`)

-- s 10(4): "At any time before or within one year (or such longer period as may be prescribed) after the date prescribed for the
-- taking of a census, if directed by the Superintendent to do so, any census officer may visit any dwelling house or other premises
-- ... for the purpose of checking any information obtained or of obtaining further information", and may correct a schedule that is
-- "incorrect in any material particular". A prescribed period shorter than one year cannot shorten it: the words are "longer".
GIVEN `months after the census date` IS A NUMBER,
      `prescribed period in months` IS A NUMBER,
      `directed by the Superintendent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a checking visit is authorised` IF
        `directed by the Superintendent`
    AND `months after the census date` AT MOST `the larger of` 12 `prescribed period in months`

-- s 7(2): an officer appointed under s 6 "must carry with him or her at all times when on duty the letter of appointment ... and
-- must produce the letter for inspection by any person who may in good faith question his or her authority".
GIVEN `appointed under section 6` IS A BOOLEAN, `questioned in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer must produce the letter of appointment` IF
    `appointed under section 6` AND `questioned in good faith`

§§ `11 and 14 -- institutions, hotels and employers`

-- s 11(1): a schedule may be delivered to "(a) every person in charge of a hospital, workhouse, prison, police station, reformatory
-- or lock-up, or of any public, charitable, religious or educational institution; (b) every keeper, secretary or manager of a hotel,
-- boarding house, lodging house or club". (2): that person must fill it in "to the best of his or her knowledge and belief" for the
-- inmates, sign it, and deliver it when required.
-- The last three places below are not in the list. That they are outside s 11 is a reading of the list, not a statement in it; their
-- residents are still reached as occupiers under s 10.
DECLARE Premises IS ONE OF
    `a hospital`
    `a prison`
    `a police lock-up`
    `a religious institution`
    `a school or other educational institution`
    `a hotel`
    `a boarding house`
    `a club`
    `a serviced apartment block`
    `a workers' dormitory`
    `an office building`

GIVEN `the premises` IS A Premises
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person in charge may be given an institutional schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the premises`
    WHEN `a serviced apartment block` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a workers' dormitory` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an office building` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 14(1): "Upon receipt of a written requisition in the prescribed form signed by the Superintendent, every employer of -- (a)
-- employees who reside in any factory or workshop; or (b) any other class or description of employees that the Minister may by
-- notification in the Gazette specify, is bound to act as an enumerator in respect of all those employees." (2): the employer must
-- have the schedule filled in "to the best of the employer's knowledge and belief" and deliver it.
GIVEN `received a signed written requisition` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `employees reside in a factory or workshop` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `employees are of a gazetted class` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the employer is bound to act as an enumerator` IF
        `received a signed written requisition`
    AND (`employees reside in a factory or workshop` OR `employees are of a gazetted class`)

§§ `13 -- information taken from other authorities`

-- s 13(1): the Superintendent may "in writing direct any competent authority specified in the first column of the First Schedule"
-- to supply particulars obtained under the law in the second column and, "despite the provisions of any written law, the competent
-- authority must furnish" them. First Schedule: the Central Provident Fund Board, under the Central Provident Fund Act 1953.
-- (2): no offence or "breach of confidence" by disclosing under such a direction.
-- (3): "Subsection (1) does not apply to any particulars or information obtained under any written law relating to taxation or
-- administered by the Monetary Authority of Singapore."
GIVEN `the authority is in the First Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `directed in writing` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained under the law named against it` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtained under a tax law or a law the MAS administers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the authority must hand the information to the Superintendent` IF
        `the authority is in the First Schedule`
    AND `directed in writing`
    AND `obtained under the law named against it`
    AND (NOT `obtained under a tax law or a law the MAS administers`)

§§ `17 and 18 -- who may see an individual's answers`

-- s 17(4): particulars "relating to any individual person obtained under the provisions of this Act must not, without the previous
-- consent in writing of that person, be disclosed except -- (a) compiled statistics on the operation of an industry may be published
-- irrespective of the number of persons engaged in that industry unless the industry is exempted by the Minister ...; (b) where the
-- disclosure can be made without identifying the individual person and, in the opinion of the Minister ..., an appropriate time has
-- elapsed; (c) for the purposes of any proceedings for an offence under this Act or any report of those proceedings; or (d)
-- information of a general nature which could be obtained from other sources."
-- s 17(3): published reports and abstracts must be arranged so that no particulars can be identified as an individual's, "except
-- with the previous consent in writing of that person".
DECLARE DisclosureGround IS ONE OF
    `the person's prior written consent`
    `the person's oral consent`
    `industry statistics, industry not exempted`
    `industry statistics, industry exempted by the Minister`
    `unidentifiable, and the Minister thinks enough time has passed`
    `unidentifiable, but the Minister does not think enough time has passed`
    `proceedings for an offence under this Act`
    `proceedings for some other offence`
    `general information obtainable elsewhere`
    `no ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A DisclosureGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 17 permits the disclosure` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `the person's prior written consent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `industry statistics, industry not exempted` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `unidentifiable, and the Minister thinks enough time has passed` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `proceedings for an offence under this Act` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `general information obtainable elsewhere` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 18(1): "Despite section 17", the Superintendent or an officer authorised in writing "may, on the written request of a
-- responsible officer of any public authority specified in the Second Schedule, disclose on a confidential basis" an individual's
-- particulars if "(a) those particulars or information could also have been obtained by the public authority under any other
-- written law; and (b) in any case where the particulars or information have been obtained from a competent authority under section
-- 13, that competent authority consents in writing". Second Schedule: the Central Provident Fund Board.
GIVEN `the authority is in the Second Schedule` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `written request by its responsible officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `disclosed by the Superintendent or an authorised officer` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `obtainable by the authority under another law` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `came from a competent authority under section 13` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `that competent authority consented in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 18 permits disclosure to the authority` IF
        `the authority is in the Second Schedule`
    AND `written request by its responsible officer`
    AND `disclosed by the Superintendent or an authorised officer`
    AND `obtainable by the authority under another law`
    AND ((NOT `came from a competent authority under section 13`) OR `that competent authority consented in writing`)

-- s 18(3): a person employed by the receiving authority "must not use any such particulars or information for the purpose of
-- enforcing any obligation or liability applicable under any written law".
GIVEN `the use is to enforce an obligation or liability` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the receiving authority's use is forbidden` IF
    `the use is to enforce an obligation or liability`

-- s 18(4): an employee of the receiving authority "who without the written approval of the Superintendent, or in breach of any
-- condition of such approval, discloses any such particulars" commits an offence: $1,000 or one month or both.
GIVEN `has the Superintendent's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `breached a condition of the approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `onward disclosure is an offence` IF
    (NOT `has the Superintendent's written approval`) OR `breached a condition of the approval`

§§ `23 -- census records in court`

-- s 23: "No entry in any book, register or record made by a census officer or by any other person in the discharge of his or her duty
-- under this Act is admissible as evidence in any civil or criminal proceedings, except in a prosecution instituted under this Act in
-- respect of any entry against the person who made the entry or caused it to be made."
DECLARE Proceeding IS ONE OF
    `a civil claim`
    `a prosecution under another Act`
    `a census prosecution of the person who made the entry`
    `a census prosecution of someone else`

GIVEN `the proceeding` IS A Proceeding
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the census entry is admissible` IF
    CONSIDER `the proceeding`
    WHEN `a census prosecution of the person who made the entry` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `18(4), 19, 20, 21 and 22 -- offences and penalties`

-- s 20: any person who "(a) refuses to answer, to the best of his or her knowledge and belief, any question asked ... by a census
-- officer which is necessary to obtain any information required for the purposes of a census; (b) knowingly makes or causes to be
-- made ... any statement which is untrue in any material particular; (c) hinders or obstructs a census officer ...; (d) removes,
-- obliterates, alters or destroys before the expiry of 6 months from the time of taking the census, any letters, marks or numbers
-- ...; (e) refuses or neglects to comply with any of the provisions of this Act or any rules ...; or (f) having possession of any
-- information which to his or her knowledge has been disclosed in contravention of the provisions of this Act, publishes or
-- communicates that information" -- $1,000 or one month or both.
-- s 19 (census officers and report staff): (a) disobeying instructions or lack of reasonable diligence; (b) "wilfully asks an
-- offensive or improper question"; (c) "knowingly makes any false return"; (d) "asks, receives or takes from any person other than an
-- authorised officer of Government any payment or reward"; (e) "without lawful authority publishes or communicates" information
-- acquired in duty -- $1,000 or one month or both.
-- s 21: "Any person who impersonates a census officer ... shall be liable on conviction to imprisonment for a term not exceeding
-- 6 months." No fine is provided; the encoding gives 0.
-- The four non-offences below are the other side of the words "necessary", "knowingly", "before the expiry of 6 months" and "to his
-- or her knowledge".
DECLARE Conduct IS ONE OF
    `refusing to answer a necessary census question`
    `refusing to answer a question not necessary for the census`
    `knowingly giving a false answer`
    `giving a wrong answer by honest mistake`
    `obstructing a census officer`
    `refusing the officer access to the premises`
    `not returning the schedule`
    `removing census marks within 6 months`
    `passing on information known to be unlawfully disclosed`
    `passing on information not known to be unlawfully disclosed`
    `an officer asking an offensive question`
    `an officer taking a tip from a householder`
    `an officer leaking an answer`
    `a public authority employee disclosing without approval`
    `impersonating a census officer`

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conduct is an offence` IF
    CONSIDER `the conduct`
    WHEN `refusing to answer a question not necessary for the census` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `giving a wrong answer by honest mistake` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `passing on information not known to be unlawfully disclosed` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine in dollars` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conduct is an offence` `the conduct` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the conduct`
         WHEN `impersonating a census officer` THEN 0
         OTHERWISE 1000

GIVEN `the conduct` IS A Conduct
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    IF NOT `the conduct is an offence` `the conduct` THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the conduct`
         WHEN `impersonating a census officer` THEN 6
         OTHERWISE 1

-- s 20(d) on its own: the marks are protected only "before the expiry of 6 months from the time of taking the census".
GIVEN `months since the census was taken` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `removing the census marks is an offence` IF
    `months since the census was taken` LESS THAN 6

-- s 22: "No prosecution shall be instituted under this Act without the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consented` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a census prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consented`
